ummary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"contnuing from #5761 .   makes no sense for a with_loader_criteria() to apply to a refresh() operaion at all. \r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Integer\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import select\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import String\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.declarative import declarative_base\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import declarative_base\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import Session\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import with_loader_criteria\r\n\r\nBase = declarative_base()\r\n\r\n\r\nclass A(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"a\"\r\n\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    data = Column(String)\r\n\r\n\r\ne = create_engine(\"sqlite://\", echo=True)\r\nBase.metadata.create_all(e)\r\n\r\ns = Session(e)\r\n\r\ns.add(A(data=\"hi\"))\r\ns.commit()\r\n\r\na1 = s.execute(\r\n    select(A)\r\n    .execution_options(populate_existing=True)\r\n    .options(with_loader_criteria(A, A.data == \"hi\"))\r\n).scalar_one()\r\n\r\ns.refresh(a1)\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nSQL:\r\n\r\n```\r\nSELECT a.id, a.data \r\nFROM a \r\nWHERE a.id = ? AND a.data = ?\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nthat's wrong, the option should be omitted, use a flag include_refresh=False.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/user